<title>UK: Standard nudges higher as SBC repeats buy.</title>
<headline>Standard nudges higher as SBC repeats buy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Standard Chartered nudged higher on Friday as brokerage SBC Warburg repeated a buy recommendation, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 1109 GMT, the shares rebounded 3-1/2p to 652-1/2p.</p>
<p>The shares stumbled yesterday, losing 10p yesterday, as Credit Lyonnais Laing cut its profit forecasts.</p>
<p>ABN-AMRO Hoare Govett said yesterday it was mulling Standard's profit prospects given the continued strength in sterling.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
